  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 124 PM MDT Mon Aug 24 2026\n\nThursday through at least Saturday, the upper ridge axis is forecast \nto shift more over the area. This should allow temperatures to be a \nbit warmer in the mid to upper 90s. The chances for 100s looks to be \nlow at this time as the ridge is forecast to deamplify as it pushes \neast. This should also lower storms chances a bit with the upper \nlevel subsidence in place. Still, it wouldn't be unreasonable for \nsome late in the day storms moving in from the west. We may also \nhave additional development in the area if the ridge deamplifies \nenough for a trough to begin to develop and push low pressure into \nthe area.\n\nFor the end of the weekend and beginning of next week, an upper \ntrough should be pushing in from the northwest. This should bring \nsome slightly cooler temperatures to the area, but probably keep \nhighs in the 80s and 90s with the trough forecast to cross the \nNorthern United States. We should also see some increase in storm \nchances with the upper level southwest flow likely assisting storms \nin developing west of the area. So in short, much of the same with \nhighs around 90 and continued storm chances.",
